## 3. Numbers vs mechanism

| Reusable algorithm | Game-specific constants |
|---|---|
| One weighted roll per phase. Each entry takes a slice of [0,1) and the rest means "nothing" | Per-stage tables (theirs, town-encounters.ts 20-79). Stage 4: nine entries at 1/20 and one at 1/40 (receipts lines 21, 28), so 0.475 chance of an encounter. Stage 12: 0.475 (nine at 1/20, one at 1/40, lines 33-42). Stage 17: 0.45 (nine at 1/20, lines 45-53). Stage 22: 0.45 (lines 56-64). Stage 27: 0.30 (six, lines 67-72). Stage 34: 0.25 (five, lines 75-79). Counts and weights from reading the table; the 0.475 etc. are sums of those weights |
| Once-per-run ledger; a repeat spends the roll | Set on the game state (theirs, game-state.ts 64) |
| Festival flag: no ledger and table normalised to its own sum | Rule name TOWN_FESTIVAL (theirs, mini-game.ts 273, 278) |
| Phase length = base + per-alive-player term + bonus for a rare event | 16000 item / 23000 portal base (theirs, stages.ts 17-18); 2000 per alive player (game-commands.ts 2062); 5000 bonus with an encounter (2065) |
| Input lockout = base (depends on rare event) + rank step x 2000, bot jitter last | 10000 / 5000 base (mini-game.ts 313); 2000 per rank step (314); stage 0 override 12000 (317); portal override 8000 (319); bot jitter 1000-6000 (325) |
| Clamp frame dt before counting timers | 50 ms (theirs, network.ts 12; applied at game-room.ts 719) |

